## 16. Known Demo Limitations

| Limitation | Detail |
|-----------|--------|
| No real payment | Checkout accepts any card — no actual charge |
| No database | All data is hardcoded TypeScript or localStorage |
| No email | Verification pages are UI only — no emails sent |
| No password hashing | Passwords stored in plaintext in the demo user array |
| File uploads not server-persisted | Product/profile images converted to base64 dataURL and stored in localStorage; cleared on browser data wipe |
| No real search backend | Search is client-side filter on in-memory array |
| No real notifications | Buyer notifications are localStorage strings; no push/email/SMS |
| Tracking notification stub | `sendTrackingNotification()` writes a localStorage record — replace the function body with an AI agent or email API for real notifications |
| Single demo seller | All checkout orders are assigned to `seller-sarah` regardless of actual product owner |
| localStorage quota | Uploading many large images may approach 5–10 MB browser storage limit; base64 is ~33% larger than the original file |
| Admin access ungated | `/admin` route has no role check in the demo — any logged-in user can navigate to it |

---

## Quick Reference — User Journeys

### Customer Journey
1. Browse `/` home page → hero, featured products, top sellers
2. Search or filter at `/products` → click product → view detail
3. Click **"Visit Store →"** on product detail to browse seller's full shop
4. Use Fit Finder / Size Guide on product detail page
5. Add to cart → open `/cart` → **select items** with checkboxes
6. Proceed to `/checkout` → fill shipping + payment → order confirmed
7. View order status and timeline in `/profile`
8. Update profile photo by hovering over avatar and clicking camera icon

### Seller Journey
1. Register at `/register` → sign in at `/signin`
2. Go to `/switch-to-selling` → complete 6-step Shop Wizard (saves progress on refresh)
3. Access `/seller` dashboard → manage overview, profile, products (with image upload), orders, payouts
4. New products start as **Pending** — wait for admin approval before appearing on the shop page
5. Process orders through OMS: pending → processing → packaged → shipped (**upload handover proof + add tracking number**) → completed
6. Request payouts from wallet; manage bank details
7. Seller shop visible at `/shop/[id]` — only approved active products shown

### Admin Journey
1. Sign in → navigate to `/admin`
2. View platform stats on Dashboard Overview
3. **Post Management** → review pending products → Approve / Reject (with comment) / Under Review
4. **Seller Management** → review seller applications, handle ban/suspend, approve sensitive profile changes, process payout requests
5. **Order Management** → view all platform orders; see "New" badge on unreviewed updates; view tracking IDs and handover proofs
6. **Customer Management** → view all customer profiles and order histories
7. Customize website banners and theme

